<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teucer</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teucer is a hero of Greek mythology, son of Telamon of Salamis and half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajax-the-great">Ajax the Great</a>, celebrated as an archer in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a>. Banished by his father after returning from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a> without Ajax, he was said to have founded the city of Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. The priest-kings of Olba in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, the Teucrids, also claimed descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teucer.jpg" alt="Teucer" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aphaia_pediment_Teukros_W-IV_Glyptothek_Munich_77.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
